 "_": [
  "FILM 5 -- Who Was Here First? (Tittira Jataka, jataka-more).",
  "",
  "THE PRIMITIVE IS `scale`, and it is the first about a RELATIONSHIP that has to hold",
  "everywhere at once. The story is an argument about size -- 'You are the biggest. That is",
  "not the same thing at all' -- so if the elephant does not dwarf the bird in every frame",
  "they share, the argument is about nothing.",
  "",
  "Heights are therefore NOT a shot's business. `rig.ladder` declares one height per",
  "character for the whole film and a layer names WHO it is:",
  "",
  "    { \"who\": \"partridge\", \"cell\": \"partridge-speak\", \"perch\": [0.42, 0.62] }",
  "",
  "`depth` scales a whole shot further away, which cannot disturb the ratios. There is no",
  "per-character height field: the drift is not discouraged, it is unsayable. film.js checks",
  "the ratios in every shot and across the film, and refuses a ladder that does not span at",
  "least 4x, because this argument has to be obvious at a glance.",
  "",
  "THE TOWER is the ending and it is carved on gateways all over India, so it has to be",
  "exactly right: each one's bottom edge IS the top edge of the one below, computed.",
  "",
  "CAST COST: zero for the monkey, two new characters (elephant, partridge) drawn once for",
  "the channel. The model sheet put all three on one ground line before a shot existed."
 ],
